<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kongsberg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kongsberg is a town in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, founded in 1624 by Christian IV after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> was discovered nearby in 1623. The Kongsberg silver mines became the largest industrial enterprise in eighteenth-century Norway and an important source of royal revenue, and the town was for a time one of Norway's largest. The mines operated until 1958, and the royal mint was based there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kongsberg.jpg" alt="Kongsberg" width="320" height="174" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mahlum · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kongsberg_Vestsida.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
